The file is written at `/Users/str/git/hub/libpcapng/bin/protos/postgresql.posa`.

Here is a summary of every design decision made:

**Structure — two GROUP members instead of one flat Object**

PostgreSQL's startup message has no leading type byte, while all subsequent messages do. A single `Object<main>` cannot handle both shapes. The `Object<PostgreSQL>` group with two members (`Startup` and `Message`) mirrors what `http.posa` does for request vs. response. The `starts "\x00\x00"` on `Startup` is the discriminator: startup-phase length fields always have 0x00 in their top two bytes (message < 65536 bytes), while regular messages start with a printable ASCII type byte (0x31–0x7A range), so there is no overlap.

**Detection rules**

Two content rules fire before the port rule:
- `tcp.content@4 "\x00\x03\x00\x00"` — v3.0 protocol version magic (same pattern used in STUN via `content@4`)
- `tcp.content@4 "\x04\xd2\x16\x2f"` — SSL request code (80877103), so SSL handshakes are captured on non-5432 ports
- `tcp.port == 5432` — fallback for sessions where the startup packet was not captured

**Startup parameters**

`repeat until "\x00"` stops iteration before consuming the list-terminating null byte (the same way `repeat until "\r\n"` stops HTTP headers before the blank line). Each iteration reads a `cstring` key and a `cstring` value; their embedded null terminators are consumed by the `cstring` type itself.

**Field types and when conditions**

All `when` conditions use decimal/hex integer literals (matching existing files like `dns.posa` and `smb.posa`). Single-character PostgreSQL type codes are commented with their ASCII equivalents. The duplicate byte 0x45 ('E') is noted — it means ErrorResponse from server and Execute from client; server-side display name wins in the enum.

**Error field repeat**

`repeat until "\x00"` with `(uint8 field_code, cstring field_value)` per item. The terminating null is left unread after the loop and will be absorbed at the next message boundary; this is the same idiom DNS uses for TXT records with `repeat until end` inside a scope.

**Coloring**

Follows the conventions in the task specification: errors white/red, ready-for-query black/lightgreen, auth and queries black/lightyellow, data rows black/lightgray, SSL/GSS white/darkblue, catch-all white/darkgray. Colors reference `postgresql.msg_type` and `postgresql.protocol` using their numeric values (as all existing color rules do).

**Aliases**

Four Wireshark-compatible aliases: `pgsql.startup.protocol`, `pgsql.type`, `pgsql.query`, `pgsql.authtype`.
